1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and it
flies on until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:29,360
To Kashiwa, the type who used to go jogging,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for staying so cheerful.

5
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow summon up some energy,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
there's only winning.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,040
One nightmare that never changes.

8
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,880
The streetscape is gentler still.

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are calling,

10
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:48,940
the sun is already setting, isn't it.

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,880
Are you going to watch
the yakitori lanterns?

12
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:11,100
Thank you for watching.

13
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,760
Reiko's cute prince

14
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,880
Senpai's late, isn't he?

15
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:36,980
The shift change time was long past already.

16
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:40,280
He's probably loafing
around somewhere again.

17
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,500
What a hopeless guy.

18
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,800
Ryo-san just arrived.

19
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,080
He just made it in time.

20
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:57,080
Haven't I always told you to keep to time?

21
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,500
When I kicked a pebble aiming at
the sunset floating over Nagagaya,

22
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:02,980
it flew all the way to Sontoru.

23
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,100
What a terrible excuse.

24
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:06,980
How shameful.

25
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:10,080
That's enough! You fool!

26
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,300
Well then, I'll be taking my leave.

27
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:13,780
Please leave the rest to you.

28
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,120
Take care.

29
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:31,820
Someone's following me.

30
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:41,420
If they keep following me,
I'll have to teach them a lesson.

31
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:05,360
Who are you?

32
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:07,620
What's wrong?

33
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,660
What are you doing out here?

34
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,720
Did you get lost or something?

35
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,860
More to the point, who are you?

36
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,180
Don't concern yourself with me.

37
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:19,000
Hey, aren't you hungry?

38
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,380
I'm not hungry.

39
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:25,880
You're hungry, aren't you?

40
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,620
I am not hungry in the slightest.

41
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:32,400
Come on, you don't have to force yourself.

42
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,780
I'm not forcing anything.

43
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,840
Just come along.

44
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,000
You'll catch a cold staying out here.

45
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,780
There's nothing to worry about.

46
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:05,540
Delicious?

47
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,820
It's very delicious, I tell you!

48
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:17,420
What's so funny?

49
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,900
No, it's just that you say
things in such an amusing way.

50
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:24,680
I'm Reiko Akimoto, a police officer.
Don't worry.

51
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,920
The world is jitterbug, jitterbug castanets!

52
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:31,380
I'll give you a reward over there.
Don't hold back!

53
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:33,520
It's fine, no need to thank me.

54
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,500
More importantly,
why were you in a place like that?

55
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:41,180
I'll give you whatever you like!

56
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,360
You must have been really exhausted.

57
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:46,700
For now, let's let him sleep.

58
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:30,500
I won't go easy on any trespassers.

59
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:47,200
Not even waking up with all this racket.

60
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:51,640
Either he's thick-skinned,
or he has nerves as steady as Ryo-chan's.

61
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:53,580
Still,

62
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,840
I wonder why they went after this kid.

63
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:06,160
What?

64
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,680
So they targeted this lost child?

65
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,540
Did a suspicious person
break into Reiko's room?

66
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:14,060
Yes, that's right.

67
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:16,760
What on earth is going on?

68
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:20,760
Kid, why are you dressed like that?

69
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,140
Are you cosplaying as a prince?

70
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:23,940
Bray-mono!

71
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,840
Bray-mono?

72
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:31,120
In short, I am Prince Chirubakasutanetto
the 17th of the Rumba Rumba Kingdom!

73
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:35,300
Hahaha, Rumba Rumba Kingdom?

74
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:37,260
Is there really a country like that?

75
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,680
I've heard of it, actually.

76
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,380
The country is small, though,

77
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:46,160
but it's known as a very rich country
that produces diamonds and rubies.

78
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:49,900
Why would a prince like that
come to Japan all by himself?

79
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:56,980
In the Rumba Rumba Kingdom,

80
00:06:57,580 --> 00:07:01,260
Duke Bossa Nova's faction is
plotting to overthrow the government!

81
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:08,100
So I, who have long wished
to visit this country,

82
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:10,080
decided to lie low here for a while,

83
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,300
but I got separated from my sheep,

84
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:14,520
and the duke's men have followed me here.

85
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,280
This creature

86
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,920
exists only in my kingdom.

87
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,660
It's the frill-necked pig Mambo.

88
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:29,460
He works as a police pig.

89
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:34,304
Do you understand? Now, from this point on,

90
00:07:34,354 --> 00:07:36,860
I shall take you into my service.

91
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:40,430
You shall protect the
world and fulfill its hopes.

92
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,820
You're happy, aren't you?

93
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,108
Mambo seems very fond of you.

94
00:07:47,158 --> 00:07:49,920
I hereby appoint you as Mambo's keeper.

95
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:50,580
What?!

96
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,365
Furthermore, I've taken a liking to you.

97
00:07:53,415 --> 00:07:55,520
Therefore, I shall make you my consort.

98
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,640
C-consort...?

99
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:01,560
This brat is proposing to Reiko at his age?!

100
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:12,460
Diamonds, rubies, sapphires.

101
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:14,540
They're all dozens of carats!

102
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,040
Nakagawa,
how much do you think they're worth?

103
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:18,120
Tens of billions, easily.

104
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,560
It's hot.

105
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:24,420
This has been passed down through
the Rumba Rumba royal family

106
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:26,580
for generations.
It's a diamond called the Star's Tear.

107
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:31,080
Take this and keep it as your dowry.

108
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:32,880
Hah, I'd be delighted!

109
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,820
Not you.

110
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,000
Senpai!

111
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,080
If I get that, I'll marry anyone,
I'll do anything!

112
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:42,460
That prince is nice, isn't he?

113
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,640
Mm, I don't mind at all.

114
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,980
I appreciate the offer, but I'm declining.

115
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:54,100
Why not? Becoming my consort
is the greatest honor there is!

116
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,320
Or are you dissatisfied with this?

117
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:03,200
That's not it. Marriage and romance
have nothing to do with money.

118
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,787
Damn it!

119
00:09:05,837 --> 00:09:09,180
Money is what makes the world go round!
Money is everything!

120
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:12,060
Ryo-chan, what are you talking about?

121
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:15,120
Back off, back off! They're backing off!

122
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:21,780
Come on, Your Highness, don't bother with these guys.
Let's go over there and play a game together, shall we?

123
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,320
Ryo-chan?

124
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:25,700
D-don't come near!

125
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,140
Come on, this way, please.

126
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,020
Come on.

127
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,260
If you show something like
that to a senior officer,

128
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:32,940
they'll lose their whole personality,
you know.

129
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:39,660
Alright, seriously.

130
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,380
Bring out the thing.

131
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:44,100
Understood, Brother Waltz.

132
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,740
Target acquired.

133
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,140
Good, fire away.

134
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:50,400
Firing now.

135
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:00,820
Can you hear me?

136
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,420
Tch, be quiet.

137
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,100
I want to go sightseeing in Tokyo.

138
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:08,920
That's right,
I came all the way to Japan, after all.

139
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:12,160
You're awfully carefree for
someone who's fled and is hiding out.

140
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:15,300
But wouldn't it be better not to
go around showing it off so much?

141
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:16,520
This.

142
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,180
Leave everything to me.

143
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:20,900
Yes.

144
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,560
I leave it to you to do as you see fit.

145
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:25,520
Ryo-chan is just doing
whatever the prince says.

146
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:28,820
At this rate,
who knows what he'll end up doing.

147
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:31,500
Fine, I'll go follow him and see.

148
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:34,820
Kei-chan, stay here on standby
in case something happens.

149
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:39,020
Understood. Please be careful.

150
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:42,940
First of all, there's no such thing as
a Shimamoto Daisaku exhibition, is there?

151
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:44,140
Do as you see fit.

152
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:47,500
This is our chance to take the prince
back to the Rumba Rumba Kingdom.

153
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:51,660
We'll get a huge reward from Duke Bossa Nova,
won't we?

154
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:52,960
Move out!

155
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,160
Cheese!

156
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,280
Whoa!

157
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:23,340
Hah!

158
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:34,700
He's not alone for a moment,
so we'll have to wait for our chance.

159
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:40,540
This is the famous Yagiri Ferry, sir.

160
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:44,220
Right this way, please.

161
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,620
Wait a second.

162
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:53,660
Busted

163
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:54,900
Prince!

164
00:11:54,900 --> 00:12:04,900
Prince!

165
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:14,960
Armin!

166
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,360
Armin!

167
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:16,780
Is anyone home!

168
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:35,880
Prince!

169
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:40,360
Someone! It won't stop!

170
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,240
Your Highness!

171
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:45,540
Eeeeeeeeh!

172
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:51,040
Whoa! Hold on tight!

173
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:53,480
Aaaaaaaah!

174
00:12:53,480 --> 00:13:00,040
Ugh... Adi!

175
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:04,980
Are you hurt? Are you all right?

176
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:09,120
Reiko, those guys are after the prince,
you know.

177
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:12,580
Still, they really went all out,
didn't they.

178
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,600
I'll just have to pay
for the damages, right?

179
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:18,820
Then, Your Highness,
I'll take care of that for you.

180
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:20,900
If you hand it over to Ryo-chan,
it's gone for good.

181
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,700
Don't say it like that.

182
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:41,500
Thank goodness nobody got hurt.

183
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:44,500
Well, then, where should we go next?

184
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:49,320
I know!
Let's go somewhere for some grown-up fun.

185
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,000
Grown-up fun.

186
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:01,020
Yeah private!

187
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,620
What grown-up fun, exactly?

188
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:08,360
No good again.

189
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:13,420
Right, next, bet on this horse.
Number six, Rumba Tambo. I like the name!

190
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:15,860
No, no,
that one's a sure bet for last place.

191
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:20,180
Here, use this. This will make him win!

192
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:22,240
Prince, is this all right?

193
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:23,820
Prince.

194
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:28,760
No, no, no. No matter how much money you pile up,
this is impossible.

195
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:31,700
We should be able to
buy this whole racetrack.

196
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,140
I don't like a prince like that.

197
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:39,000
You can't solve everything with money.

198
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:45,300
There are many things in this
world more important than money.

199
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:46,660
I want you to understand that.

200
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:49,460
Shut up. I don't want to hear a sermon.

201
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:51,640
The prince!

202
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,040
Hey, wait!

203
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,240
Did you find him?

204
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:14,200
Your master really causes a lot of trouble,
doesn't he?

205
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:49,320
It went off without a hitch, Waltz, bro.

206
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:53,400
Lord Waltz's plan is flawless.

207
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:56,840
All we have to do is get the prince on tonight's ship,
and the mission's complete.

208
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,820
Prince, please bear with us for a while.

209
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:04,440
Snap out of it, Mambo!

210
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:06,920
He's the police pig of the
Rumba Rumba Kingdom, right?

211
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:11,700
What's wrong?

212
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,000
What's got you worried?

213
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:21,440
Senior Reiko,
something terrible has happened!

214
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:23,400
What is it, Kei-chan?

215
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:28,260
An international sniper has apparently
sneaked into Japan to target Prince Jilba.

216
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:32,340
An international sniper? You mean a hitman?

217
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:36,120
Yes, that famous Fuga 13!

218
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,880
Pyah, pyah, pyah!

219
00:16:42,590 --> 00:16:46,120
Chase him, chase him!

220
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:49,920
I'll definitely take him down.

221
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:54,880
That's me, Fuga 13.

222
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:55,280
Ting!

223
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,040
Don't stand behind me!

224
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:05,560
Coming, coming, coming!

225
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:08,020
Is it already this late?

226
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:09,880
Match, it's your turn to relieve me.

227
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:14,640
What are you talking about? Match, look!

228
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,480
The prince is running away!

229
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:20,640
Idiot, you comrade idiot!

230
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,140
This song...

231
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,980
Arty! If you're here, that means...

232
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,660
Yes, the plan has changed.

233
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:32,840
We've called off capturing the prince.

234
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,200
I'll take care of him myself.

235
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,840
You're all out. You're through.

236
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:40,520
Big Brother Waltz.

237
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:50,060
I am hungry.

238
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:56,460
Hey, this bean paste...
even its tail has been eaten away!

239
00:17:56,460 --> 00:18:02,500
You there, hand that over to me!
What, you bastard? This one's mine. My da...

240
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:08,740
I'll give you an example! Hey, I just want what's mine.
Don't be so greedy!

241
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,360
Geez, we finally made it, you numbskull!

242
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,360
It was delicious.

243
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:25,340
Reiko's cookies.

244
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,540
Hold on tight.

245
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:33,260
Reiko is a wonderful woman.

246
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:34,260
And yet,

247
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:35,940
I caused you trouble.

248
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:39,840
Not everything can be solved with money.

249
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:41,060
In this world,

250
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,740
there are many things
more important than money.

251
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,600
I want you to understand that.

252
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:49,720
Reiko is right.

253
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:52,580
Damn it!

254
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,400
Money is everything in this world!
Money is all that matters!

255
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,760
That man is living the wrong way, isn't he.

256
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:02,600
Quick! Quick! Quick!

257
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:05,820
Chase them, chase them!

258
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:16,900
Right, if it comes to this,
at least we get the prince's Star Droplet!

259
00:19:21,300 --> 00:19:23,300
Hurry, Mambo! The prince is in danger!

260
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,780
Looks like he was definitely here.

261
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:28,020
He should be nearby.

262
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:39,340
Ugh, Gorza!

263
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:41,740
Wait!

264
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:47,860
Gh, who's that?

265
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:53,800
Wee!

266
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:55,980
Wee!

267
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:57,060
There he is!

268
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:57,680
Prince!

269
00:19:58,660 --> 00:20:01,060
You've gone and made a mess again!

270
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:04,180
Kill!

271
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:05,740
Aaaaaah!

272
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:08,240
Aaaaaah!

273
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:22,680
Aaaaaah!

274
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:52,260
Reiko!

275
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,860
Watch out!

276
00:20:56,860 --> 00:21:00,180
Aaaaaah!

277
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:17,140
I was wrong.

278
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,300
Whoa!

279
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:19,380
Aaaaaah!

280
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,720
You must be hungry, right?

281
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:25,700
Shh!

282
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:27,780
Yeah.

283
00:21:30,380 --> 00:21:35,100
No, no, not to Ryo-chan, no way.

284
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:37,040
Prince, I'm glad you're safe.

285
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:41,700
Good work.

286
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:44,360
Today's success belongs to Reiko.

287
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:48,120
Your Highness, I'm glad you're safe.

288
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:51,740
Reiko, my butler Sutara, is here.

289
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:53,380
Please rejoice.

290
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:57,360
The entire Bossa Nova Duke
gang has been arrested.

291
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,600
I see.

292
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:00,300
You can rest easy now.

293
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:02,740
You can return to the
Kingdom of Rumba Rumba.

294
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:06,040
And now, distinguished guests,

295
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:10,520
Prince Jilba Castanet
XVII will now address you.

296
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:16,940
We are deeply grateful for your attendance
at today's farewell party of the century.

297
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:22,080
The friendship between Japan and the
Kingdom of Rumba Rumba will last forever.

298
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:26,640
Yes, well, I, Jilba Castanet,

299
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:30,420
though my stay in Japan this time was brief,

300
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:33,860
I learned things I will never
forget for the rest of my life.

301
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:36,020
When I return to my country,

302
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:38,720
I will draw strength from this
precious experience and these memories

303
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:42,720
and I swear to become a fine
king beloved by all my people.

304
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:45,760
And now, the prince himself

305
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:48,440
will shake hands with each of you,

306
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:51,180
and we would like to make
this our final farewell.

307
00:22:58,700 --> 00:22:59,400
Reiko...

308
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:01,580
Prince, this is for you.

309
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:06,680
Become a wonderful king, okay?

310
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,680
He's really gone

311
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:18,380
Yeah.

312
00:23:18,380 --> 00:23:22,180
It was just like Roman Holiday, wasn't it?

313
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:24,760
A Kameari holiday

314
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:26,260
Wee!

315
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:30,540
It's Mambo!
Did you miss the plane or something?

316
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:31,620
Wee.

317
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:34,440
Nakagawa, charter a jet right away!

318
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:36,220
We're taking Mambo to him!

319
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:37,400
Heh heh heh.

320
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:41,480
Now it's our turn for a
Rumba Rumba royal holiday!

321
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:50,400
It's as if someone is calling,

322
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:53,140
an afternoon after the rain.

323
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:59,520
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand of Gacha.

324
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:06,820
That strange feeling I had back then.

325
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:11,960
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

326
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:17,720
I tried walking only on the black ones.

327
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:25,900
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

328
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:33,340
Even the politicians with their pompous faces
and the aunties who are a thorn in the eye.

329
00:24:33,870 --> 00:24:44,100
Turn that corner, come on,
you'll meet everyone, everyone.

330
00:24:44,100 --> 00:24:52,100
There's Kameari over there
surely there's Kameari.

331
00:24:52,620 --> 00:24:57,380
Everyone, come on over to our town.

332
00:24:57,380 --> 00:25:05,300
There's Kameari over there
surely there's Kameari.

333
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:10,440
Everyone, come on over to our town.

334
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:17,820
I'm starving, feed me something!

335
00:25:17,820 --> 00:25:19,720
All-you-can-eat sounds good.

336
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:21,680
Sushi, yakiniku, or crab?

337
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:22,940
What, strawberries?

338
00:25:22,940 --> 00:25:25,600
Will this fill up a grown man's belly?

339
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,980
Hold on, there's something that
looks even tastier over there!

340
00:25:28,980 --> 00:25:31,740
Next time: men's strawberry picking.

341
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:32,620
See you then.

342
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:35,840
Over there is Kameary.

343
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:39,980
Yeah, it's definitely Kameary.

344
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:44,220
Everyone, come on over to our town!

345
00:25:45,100 --> 00:25:45,780
Thank you.

